      "content": "What you're describing—feeling detached or numb in a critical moment—is a very real experience and doesn't define your entire worth. These moments of inaction are often symptoms of deeper struggles, not evidence of a character defect. It takes immense courage to acknowledge this feeling, and recognizing it is the first step toward understanding it. A therapist can help you unpack these moments and understand the roots of that detachment.",
      "source": "target",
