      "content": "It's true that the void feels like your entire reality right now, but that feeling is a temporary state, not a permanent truth about who you are. Comparing yourself to others is a trap that only deepens the sense of inadequacy, because everyone has their own invisible struggles. Instead of seeing yourself as a mistake, try viewing this emptiness as an invitation to explore what you actually *want* to feel or do. You have inherent value simply by existing, even if you can't feel it right now.",
